    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d146">

                <pb facs="0277" n="111" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg111"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/2741</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Reinsch to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-21T20:00:00+08:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 21, 1917, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Prime Minister has again resigned. Have reliable information to the effect
                    that all Ministers will resign tomorrow. General Wang Shi-chen, Chief of Staff
                    has been appointed Minister of War and will become Prime Minister after
                    arranging a new Cabinet. Meanwhile Tien, ex-governor Honan, will act. It is
                    expected Kuo Min Tang will participate new Government with Chihli party. Status
                    of communication party uncertain. Tsao spared no efforts to be kept. The change
                    is considered wholesome as the present Government rested on too narrow a
                    foundation. It is probable that Parliament will be convened speedily.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
